{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate","id":840252,"title":"Dominate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-01T16:52:45-08:00","id":840252,"title":"Dominate","content":"I started a new Vampire chronicle. Unlike in the last one, one of the PCs is a Ventrue. He took Dominate at 3 dots on chargen, and is rather fond of solving problems with it. The problem with it is that it works... and a little too well, at that. Some things he was able to do with it include:<ul><li>Force someone to open a door to their house in the middle of the night and then stand still and silently afterwards (he caught their eye through a peeping hole).</li> <li>Make someone recall memories another vampire had made them forget. This one actually pushed the plot forward, so I'm not entirely complaining.</li> <li>Have a random person off the street watch a building for him all night.</li> </ul>\u200bHis dice pool on the first-dot power is so big that no one can really resist it. Am I being too lenient here, and it shouldn't be so easy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:58:58-08:00","id":840256,"title":"","content":"Those are kind of minor things. Though unless he got the first person to forget what happened they're going to be asking a lot of questions, and the third person might have simply missed something unless they were watching every angle of a building and had a high perception score and some sort of method of seeing through magical stealth.<br /> <br /> If you have important NPCs you want to introduce and not have them be susceptible to it give them some higher resistance scores..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:02:12-08:00","id":840258,"title":"","content":"Only the second use of Dominate was actually helpful, yes. In the first instance, breaking into that apartment got them no information, but the mess they made tipped their enemies off. In the third instance, nothing of note happened in that building. I'm just rather put off by how easy it is to have an NPC do what you want for a whole scene. Even for a vampire, there's only so much a good resistance score can do, unless they also have high BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:06:33-08:00","id":840260,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty much like what Dominate is supposed to do, to me. Also, it seems like in scenario 3 he's making a pretty big gamble that this random dude off the street will be... Uh, any good at watching this building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:08:25-08:00","id":840261,"title":"","content":"It just takes one slip to notice things. A vampire probably isn't going to appreciate another trying to dominate them. I believe there's also an Iron Will merit somewhere. My players used dominate to steal cars to get places. It's fun to use dominate, there's a sense of power and monstrousness in being a vampire. What use is a mind controlling vampire who can't mind control people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:08:27-08:00","id":840262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840258#post840258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the second use of Dominate was actually helpful, yes. In the first instance, breaking into that apartment got them no information, but the mess they made tipped their enemies off. In the third instance, nothing of note happened in that building. I'm just rather put off by how easy it is to have an NPC do what you want for a whole scene. Even for a vampire, there's only so much a good resistance score can do, unless they also have high BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to resist: Give them an ungodly Lashing Out pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:10:17-08:00","id":840264,"title":"","content":"If you know how Dominate works, it's super easy to dodge it. You have at least one opportunity to act between Vampire Dominating you and declaring their command. Taking any amount of damage from any source removes Mesmerized, so if your target is hurt in the space between you completing the power and commanding them, the spell is broken.<br /> Using combat turns, it looks like this:<br /> Round 1:<br /> Dominator: Dominate as a Instant Action<br /> Everyone else: Still have their actions<br /> Round 2:<br /> Dominator: Issue the Command as a Instant Action<br /> Dominated person: OBEY<br /> <br /> This means that particularly determined vampire, or even mortal, can make your players go O__O by using his action to punch or stab himself to break the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:18:07-08:00","id":840274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840260#post840260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems pretty much like what Dominate is supposed to do, to me. Also, it seems like in scenario 3 he's making a pretty big gamble that this random dude off the street will be... Uh, any good at watching this building.</div> </div> </div> </div>It did end up being pretty tremendously unhelpful, yes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840261#post840261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just takes one slip to notice things. A vampire probably isn't going to appreciate another trying to dominate them. I believe there's also an Iron Will merit somewhere. My players used dominate to steal cars to get places. It's fun to use dominate, there's a sense of power and monstrousness in being a vampire. What use is a mind controlling vampire who can't mind control people?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and I've been having NPCs make note of the character's tendency to use Dominate as a blunt instrument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840262#post840262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't need to resist: Give them an ungodly Lashing Out pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about Lashing Out, I'll admit. Does it work to counter mental/social disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840264#post840264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you know how Dominate works, it's super easy to dodge it. You have at least one opportunity to act between Vampire Dominating you and declaring their command. Taking any amount of damage from any source removes Mesmerized, so if your target is hurt in the space between you completing the power and commanding them, the spell is broken.<br /> Using combat turns, it looks like this:<br /> Round 1:<br /> Dominator: Dominate as a Instant Action<br /> Everyone else: Still have their actions<br /> Round 2:<br /> Dominator: Issue the Command as a Instant Action<br /> Dominated person: OBEY<br /> <br /> This means that particularly determined vampire, or even mortal, can make your players go O__O by using his action to punch or stab himself to break the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point as well, if not applicable to those situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:24:03-08:00","id":840276,"title":"","content":"It's a good safety option for things like &quot;let's Dominate major vampire npc and go wild with it&quot;, I feel.<br /> As for minor dominates, eh, consider them as lifestyle changes and embrace them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:45:59-08:00","id":840284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840262#post840262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't need to resist: Give them an ungodly Lashing Out pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can Lash Out against Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:53:25-08:00","id":840288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840264#post840264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This means that particularly determined vampire, or even mortal, can make your players go O__O by using his action to punch or stab himself to break the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can the mesmerized person even act? I'm not sure they can. While it says they don't act like they're obviously hypnotized, their will has still been made subordinate to the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:11:28-08:00","id":840292,"title":"","content":"They can. They are &quot;little quieter&quot; than usual, though. I'm pretty sure that it's written this way specifically to make sure that Dominate isn't trivializing physical conflicts - it's spelled out that you need to take multiple rounds to use the power and then issue command(s). Which is a great balancing act, because in combat people *will* continue to try and gut you while you are talking them down, and outside of combat, only people who understand how Dominate works and have firsthand experience with it should reliably abuse that space of time.<br /> It's doubly tricky to remember how being mesmerized feels, because you don't remember it after you stop being mesmerized! But a high ranking vampire probably asked someone to Dominate him, and then order him to remember how mesmerize feels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-01-2016, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:20:53-08:00","id":840296,"title":"","content":"They're a little quieter and more reserved than normal. Hitting themselves with enough force to cause injury doesn't seem quiet or reserved to me. It really seems more like it's made the way it is so <i>other people</i> can snap the mesmerized character out of it than a singular opponent being able to snap themselves out of it. The original target seems to be totally hypnotized, they just don't outwardly appear to be so. I may be wrong, but that's how it reads to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:38:45-08:00","id":840301,"title":"","content":"Sure. The intent is definitely so that you can't just mesmerize people in middle of combat and deny turns to them. In practice, all mesmerize does is making target character vulnerable to your next command. Due to the fact that a) you have a space of time between being mesmerized and receiving the command, and b) damage breaking it, it isn't a very practical combat power. Which is working as intended, because I remember that whenever Dominate popped up in previous incarnations of Vampire, people complained it was way too powerful and undefendable-from. <br /> Accidentally, this balancing feature creates a situation where someone can punch themselves to break free before receiving an order - which I find cool. Again, it's not something to abuse to deny players the power - it's more something to pull out when the target is a experienced individual; one of Ventrue themselves or a jaded, veteran hunter, for example. Note that not many people will *know* that they are mesmerized, and even fewer will know that grabbing that pen and slamming it into your knee will snap you out of vampire's mind control <br /> As for being totally hypnotized - dunno, IMHO mesmerized is simply *potential* to being controlled (which is exploited by issuing the command, and thus completing the spell). Full hypnosis is more like Dominated, which is escalated version of Mesmerized - thing that you can turn Mesmerized into if you have more dots in Dominate and even more time on your hands to play with the victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:42:30-08:00","id":840304,"title":"","content":"I agree with Ashenrogue. I'm quite sure that the description says that they don't seems hypnotized but just more reserved unless the command you give is something that the dominated nevere do. Like kill or something else.<br /> I always seen domination works letting, with the eyes contact, the victim quite and ready to recive the command. Then he don't remember anything and executes the order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:53:41-08:00","id":840313,"title":"","content":"Thing is, hypnosis doesn't star until you give them the command - being Mesmerized isn't equal to being commanded. Mesmerized is scene-long *potential* for being hypnotized. You need to issue an actual command first for the victim to get all YES MY LORD. And I'm talking about the space between you using your first dot and issuing the command.<br /> I mean, you can go meet a dude, shake hands with him, quietly Mesmerize his two bodyguards between one business proposal and another, and then - if you find that you need them to break the dude's legs after he decides that he is taking both his moneys and your drugs - order them to break the guy's legs instead of killing you. Or you might complete your deal without problems, and the condition will short out harmlessly after the scene ends.<br /> You cannot resist the command, but you are not a vegetable waiting for the command to happen, either.<br /> EDIT<br /> Like, drooling vegetable is probably the Exceptional Success resolution for the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-01-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T19:00:31-08:00","id":840316,"title":"","content":"No, I'm fairly certain you're hypnotized the instant you're mesmerized. While it isn't outwardly apparent you've been hypnotized, you definitely are indeed under vampire hypnosis even before they give you a command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T19:08:15-08:00","id":840320,"title":"","content":"I can agree with that as long as &quot;hypnotized&quot; is &quot;you cannot obey commands given to you by this vampire [but are free to proceed normally other than that]&quot;, not &quot;a drooling vegetable waiting for commands&quot;. You need to talk to the victim to make them obey your bidding. No talking, no control. No commands, victim processes as normal. Spend your 4 words per command wisely.<br /> Notice the fluff on the discipline, too - it's all about your voice and the way Beats modulates your words, not the psychic link. That's also why you use Expression in the dice pool instead of something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T19:19:28-08:00","id":840327,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure it's more like as long as you're &quot;hypnotized&quot; &quot;you cannot disobey orders given to you by the vampire [you can act relatively freely as long as you remain quiet and subdued]&quot;.<br /> <br /> Attacking anything, yourself included, is definitely not subdued behavior. So while you can probably walk around fine, and maybe even have a quiet conversation with someone else, anything more than that is beyond you until you shed the condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:25:36-08:00","id":840353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840264#post840264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you know how Dominate works, it's super easy to dodge it. You have at least one opportunity to act between Vampire Dominating you and declaring their command. Taking any amount of damage from any source removes Mesmerized, so if your target is hurt in the space between you completing the power and commanding them, the spell is broken.<br /> Using combat turns, it looks like this:<br /> Round 1:<br /> Dominator: Dominate as a Instant Action<br /> Everyone else: Still have their actions<br /> Round 2:<br /> Dominator: Issue the Command as a Instant Action<br /> Dominated person: OBEY<br /> <br /> This means that particularly determined vampire, or even mortal, can make your players go O__O by using his action to punch or stab himself to break the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind if Celerity is on the field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:35:32-08:00","id":840467,"title":"","content":"As a rule, it seems like the intended design of 2e is for mortals to effectively be at the mercy of any vampire that wants to do something to them, barring exceptional individuals who happen to be rolling lucky.<br /> <br /> The primary weaknesses of Dominate have already been mentioned. Memories need wiped, for one, unless you're careful. Damage can/does break it. There are limits to what can be done with the lower dots. There might be witnesses outside of your target (a camera sees the security guard unlocking and opening the door for someone; even if the Beast keeps the Vampire from being recognized in the film, the guard will likely end up fired before any longer-term commands can be followed).<br /> <br /> But, in general, you should expect a Ventrue to do what Ventrue do with common mortals. If you don't want it to work, it'll either be an exceptional individual (high stats and/or resistance merits) or another vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:03:37-08:00","id":840515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate#post840252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started a new Vampire chronicle. Unlike in the last one, one of the PCs is a Ventrue. He took Dominate at 3 dots on chargen, and is rather fond of solving problems with it. The problem with it is that it works... and a little too well, at that. Some things he was able to do with it include:<ul><li>Force someone to open a door to their house in the middle of the night and then stand still and silently afterwards (he caught their eye through a peeping hole).</li> <li>Make someone recall memories another vampire had made them forget. This one actually pushed the plot forward, so I'm not entirely complaining.</li> <li>Have a random person off the street watch a building for him all night.</li> </ul><br /> \u200bHis dice pool on the first-dot power is so big that no one can really resist it. Am I being too lenient here, and it shouldn't be so easy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What exactly is the problem? Except for pulling up memories explicitly made to be forgotten (personally I wouldn't allow it without a devotion or exceptional success on Lying Mind) which can arguably be done by someone with Auspex 3 (depending on how infallible the ST allows Auspex to be) all of this is stuff that can be done by a vampire using Majesty 1 or someone waving around a stack of 50s.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:07:52-08:00","id":840516,"title":"","content":"I think that, when in the description of the mesmerized condition it says: &quot;You\u2019re not obviously hypnotized \u2014 you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary.&quot;, it is written with the intention to not let the use of mesmerize power, obvious to other observers. For exemple you could use it in an elysium or during a dinner with other diners, and mesmerize a particular person without other think something strange is happening.<br /> In the example of the combat, using Mesmerize on the opponent, according to my personal interpretation of the power (after the appropriate roll to catch the eyes of the victim), lets him quiet and he stops to attack anyone unless, someone else, attack him dealing any damage.<br /> Probably I'm wrong but I like the idea that the vampire's gaze lets the opponent.....mesmerized and in his power even before the mechanical act of speacking and impress the order.<br /> So probably 1v1, if the opponent is not a vampire (or have a low resistance pool), it could be a strong power, but there are a lot more effective power to stop the fighting...<br /> Just think about Obfuscate, disappear and hit the enemy with a backstab that ignore defense and deal a Killing Blow. And this power acts immediately not in two turns. Even the simple celerity, that allow you to interrupt the enemy action or put you on the top of initiative.<br /> So I don't see why Domination should be out of these range of effect. It's absolutely not unbalanced in these way I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:11:20-08:00","id":840520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840515#post840515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What exactly is the problem? Except for pulling up memories explicitly made to be forgotten (personally I wouldn't allow it without a devotion or exceptional success on Lying Mind) which can arguably be done by someone with Auspex 3 (depending on how infallible the ST allows Auspex to be) all of this is stuff that can be done by a vampire using Majesty 1 or someone waving around a stack of 50s.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a Clash of Wills to me.. so hardly any reliable if the one who made the memories dissapear is any competent, and if they're not - all is well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:14:30-08:00","id":840523,"title":"","content":"Sounds like it's time to introduce a Strix or two. With Indomitable. Get him to think outside the box a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:49:53-08:00","id":840534,"title":"","content":"So I guess the common consensus is that this is Dominate working as intended, and I should account for that. I've already had the PC acquire something of a reputation for being very trigger-happy with Dominate. Other vampires and ghouls are going to be careful when dealing with him. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840467#post840467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule, it seems like the intended design of 2e is for mortals to effectively be at the mercy of any vampire that wants to do something to them, barring exceptional individuals who happen to be rolling lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, I certainly hope this isn't the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:35:26-08:00","id":840550,"title":"","content":"It's true as far as random schmucks on the street go. Humans that can stand up to vampires are moderately uncommon, but not so much that there's not a good chance of running into one. If a vampire is isn't careful they will get their ass handed to them sooner or later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T05:16:09-08:00","id":840568,"title":"","content":"It probably won't come up in this chronicle, anyway. The antagonists are vampires, and the players decided not to follow up on a potential plan that'd require killing a mortal criminal. They became more careful after I made them roll for detachment after the stunt described in the first situation.<br /> <br /> Mind you, vampires aren't <i>that </i>much more resilient against Dominate. They add their Blood Potency to the resistance roll, but for many that'll be just one or two dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 03-02-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:50:57-08:00","id":840612,"title":"","content":"Thus, Strix. Have it just flat out not work one guy and see if anyone figures out why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:03:54-08:00","id":840662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840515#post840515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is the problem? Except for pulling up memories explicitly made to be forgotten (personally I wouldn't allow it without a devotion or exceptional success on Lying Mind) which can arguably be done by someone with Auspex 3 (depending on how infallible the ST allows Auspex to be) all of this is stuff that can be done by a vampire using Majesty 1 or someone waving around a stack of 50s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lay Open the Mind explicitly allows for calling up memories hidden by magic with a Clash of Wills, so I don't really think an ST ruling is needed there. The Lying Mind explicitly doesn't allow a vampire to read memories. You could command them to tell you their memories, but you don't get direct access with Dominate. Lying Mind doesn't even get a roll, so you can't exceptionally succeed on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:13:54-08:00","id":840666,"title":"","content":"I allowed it to happen primarily because I needed it to get the plot going. It's always tricky to get the PCs on the right track in an investigative story. Now that they've got a clear goal and more options, I can't really do that anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:04:22-08:00","id":840698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840284#post840284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can Lash Out against Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div> You can't. You can lash out against all of Majesty, and half of Nightmare 1 (the non-illusion creating part). No other Discipline is affected by Lashing Out. I'm not even sure if you can Lash Out against some of the Majesty devotions!<br /> <br /> As for the hypnosis thing, I agree with Ashen - the moment Dominate 1 goes off, you are hypnotized and primed for recieving orders.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd, yeah, pretty much your players are running Dominate as its intended to go. Werewolves are specialists at the hunt. Mages are awesome at digging up information. Demons are kick ass with the spycraft. Vampires are specialists in mind control. They're hands down the best at mind controlling, even more so than any mage, changeling, werewolf, demon, beast, prommie, whatever. This is what vampires do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:48:05-08:00","id":840769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840516#post840516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, when in the description of the mesmerized condition it says: &quot;You\u2019re not obviously hypnotized \u2014 you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary.&quot;, it is written with the intention to not let the use of mesmerize power, obvious to other observers. For exemple you could use it in an elysium or during a dinner with other diners, and mesmerize a particular person without other think something strange is happening.<br /> In the example of the combat, using Mesmerize on the opponent, according to my personal interpretation of the power (after the appropriate roll to catch the eyes of the victim), lets him quiet and he stops to attack anyone unless, someone else, attack him dealing any damage.<br /> Probably I'm wrong but I like the idea that the vampire's gaze lets the opponent.....mesmerized and in his power even before the mechanical act of speacking and impress the order.<br /> So probably 1v1, if the opponent is not a vampire (or have a low resistance pool), it could be a strong power, but there are a lot more effective power to stop the fighting...<br /> Just think about Obfuscate, disappear and hit the enemy with a backstab that ignore defense and deal a Killing Blow. And this power acts immediately not in two turns. Even the simple celerity, that allow you to interrupt the enemy action or put you on the top of initiative.<br /> So I don't see why Domination should be out of these range of effect. It's absolutely not unbalanced in these way I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I'd originally envisioned it. Though I'll admit the reading that characters can break out by hurting themselves immediately is pretty cool, and sets up for some great antagonists.<br /> <br /> However, it's something I'd caution storytellers against using. Mesmerized isn't an obvious condition, the victim has no idea they've been affected. So the only sort of person who would stab himself to break mesmerize is a) someone with an Unseen Sense for Discipline use or b) Someone so paranoid that they believe eye contact is dangerous. In the latter case this character would likely never make eye contact and stab himself frequently out of sheer paranoia that someone had secretly mesmerized him, which is the sure sign of a deeply unsound mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Indeed, the only reasonable narrative explanation for being able to act on Mesmerism so quickly (barring Unseen Sense) is that the character <b>immediately </b>injures themselves every time they meet eyes with the vampire. Anything else would be aggressive power gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-02-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:57:58-08:00","id":840780,"title":"","content":"Disciplines are generally considered to be subtle powers. Or at least that's the impression I got from speaking with the writers. So, anytime someone says that they instantly detect the use of some mental power? I generally call shinannigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:23:43-08:00","id":840836,"title":"","content":"Well, I did have a ghoul who approached the players recognize that the PC was trying to dominate him the instant he didn't comply with their wishes. But that was to the players' benefit, as otherwise the group the ghoul belonged to would've refused to deal with them altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:40:37-08:00","id":840846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840769#post840769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b) Someone so paranoid that they believe eye contact is dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Isn't it</i>, though? I mean, we are talking about vampires. Ideally, you never look at them with your naked eyes if you could help it (such as looking at the monitor of a live video feed instead).<br /> <br /> And if you don't know you are confronting Vampires, well, you're at a disadvantage no matter which way you look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:46:45-08:00","id":840896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840846#post840846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Isn't it</i>, though? I mean, we are talking about vampires. Ideally, you never look at them with your naked eyes if you could help it (such as looking at the monitor of a live video feed instead).<br /> <br /> And if you don't know you are confronting Vampires, well, you're at a disadvantage no matter which way you look at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which vampire? You can't just lump all vampires, even all Ventrue, under the sociopathic scheming lunatic heading. Sure there will be certain vampiric antagonists so menacing or ill reputed that characters never meet their eyes. But on the whole it's rather paranoid to assume every vampire you meet will immediately subvert your will.<br /> <br /> Really its a narrative thing. Dan Hellsign, professional vampire hunter, conspiracy theorist, and gun toting quack? He'd never make eye contact with a vampire, or perhaps with anyone for that matter. But Deborah Slant, bartender and ghoul lover of the local Prince probably wouldn't think twice of looking a vampire in the eye. <br /> <br /> Basically, different experiences breed different reactions. Which is good, and realistic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:10:16-08:00","id":840912,"title":"","content":"Well, yes. But it also depends upon capabilities and trust. Your ghoul example has a Prince backing them. Average ghoul meeting with a vampire they know nothing about? Probably better to keep off eye contact. It's rude, maybe, but an understandable precaution. While all vampires aren't the same, they all have the <i>potential</i> to Dominate. Making eye contact, knowing that, is a sign of trust and/or confidence. <hr /><br /> ...And now this topic has given me the idea for a Hunter Conspiracy that ritually blinds themselves (either permanently, or via headgear) and uses their Endowment for &quot;sight beyond sight&quot; to seek out the monsters that hide behind a veil of humanity. The Dominate resistance would just be a side bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:28:27-08:00","id":840923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840896#post840896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which vampire? You can't just lump all vampires, even all Ventrue, under the sociopathic scheming lunatic heading. Sure there will be certain vampiric antagonists so menacing or ill reputed that characters never meet their eyes. But on the whole it's rather paranoid to assume every vampire you meet will immediately subvert your will.<br /> <br /> Really its a narrative thing. Dan Hellsign, professional vampire hunter, conspiracy theorist, and gun toting quack? He'd never make eye contact with a vampire, or perhaps with anyone for that matter. But Deborah Slant, bartender and ghoul lover of the local Prince probably wouldn't think twice of looking a vampire in the eye.<br /> <br /> Basically, different experiences breed different reactions. Which is good, and realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>My werewolf has seen a vampire turn invisible and try and fail to order his mind around, plus the blood stuff. So he's fairly sure that's what all vampires can do, as he is unaware of the concept of clans. Her shapeshifting is new, however. Fortunately their scent gives them away really easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:28:38-08:00","id":840924,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; Sounds like a Clash of Wills to me.. so hardly any reliable if the one who made the memories disappear is any competent, and if they're not - all is well. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Dominate doesn't allow you to undo memory alteration in 2nd edition. Changes are permanent. I can see allowing someone else using careful wording of dominate commands while someone is mesmerized could possibly be allowed for them to recite their true memories but since dominate carries a maximum word count and you don't recall what you did while mesmerized (thus retaining the premise that altered memories are permanent) that's pretty tricky hence the exceptional success requirement.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; Lay Open the Mind explicitly allows for calling up memories hidden by magic with a Clash of Wills, so I don't really think an ST ruling is needed there. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> I deliberately said Auspex 3, not Auspex 4. And I also said that it depends on how infallible STs allow Auspex to be, all they would have to do is put their hands on the person with the altered memory, ask a relevant question about what happened and they'll get a vision on what really happened, not the false memories that are recalled.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; Lying Mind doesn't even get a roll, so you can't exceptionally succeed on it. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Lying Mind must be used on a victim who they mesmerized first, so yes you technically can get an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-02-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:55:09-08:00","id":840933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840846#post840846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Isn't it</i>, though? I mean, we are talking about vampires. Ideally, you never look at them with your naked eyes if you could help it (such as looking at the monitor of a live video feed instead).<br /> <br /> And if you don't know you are confronting Vampires, well, you're at a disadvantage no matter which way you look at it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But at p.131 is written:<br /> <br /> &quot;Success: The vampire holds her victim\u2019s gaze for just a second,<br /> but it\u2019s enough to inflict the Mesmerized Condition&quot;<br /> <br /> It's really difficult to not cross the gazes for just a second, even if the targhet try to avoid it actively. I would make at least a contested roll based on wits+??? (I don't know the appropriate skill) to see if the victim manages to avoid the eyes contact.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:22:22-08:00","id":840976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840923#post840923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My werewolf has seen a vampire turn invisible and try and fail to order his mind around, plus the blood stuff. So he's fairly sure that's what all vampires can do, as he is unaware of the concept of clans. Her shapeshifting is new, however. Fortunately their scent gives them away really easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if wolf senses can cause a clash of wills, but if they can't, you can't smell the scent of a Vampire using Obfuscate 3(Cloak of Night, who turns the vampire invisible).<br /> Cloak of Night makes you vanish, produce no sound and no smell.<br /> <br /> ON Topic:<br /> Lashing out can end a command from Dominate?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:42:11-08:00","id":841002,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm concerned about is that when the PCs need to extract information from a neonate (as a favour for some characters who have the information they need), the Ventrue will just Dominate him into telling them who his sire is. Kind of cuts the whole thing short. The best &quot;counter&quot; I've come up with is for the PC in question to acquire a reputation for overusing Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 03-02-2016, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T17:10:40-08:00","id":841013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840976#post840976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can't smell the scent of a Vampire using Obfuscate 3(Cloak of Night, who turns the vampire invisible).<br /> Cloak of Night makes you vanish, produce no sound and no smell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are signs of your presence left, but otherwise you're correct.<br /> <br /> There are abilities that let them cause a clash of wills, but she did not demonstrate all her skills at the same time, the scent was not noticeable while she was invisible, just before and after, and months later after the shapechanging.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T19:29:24-08:00","id":841064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841002#post841002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm concerned about is that when the PCs need to extract information from a neonate (as a favour for some characters who have the information they need), the Ventrue will just Dominate him into telling them who his sire is. Kind of cuts the whole thing short. The best &quot;counter&quot; I've come up with is for the PC in question to acquire a reputation for overusing Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but as the dominator has this weapon, the sire has his own weapon as well to use in order to conceal his plans. For example he could change the memory of his neonate if him were captured, putting the Ventrue astray. Or command to him, with dominate, to not talk or lie about something. In this case the Ventrue should win a clash of will comparing the successes of the neonate's sire with his own. And if the sire is an elder probably wins the contested roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:14:36-08:00","id":841081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840924#post840924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;&lt; Lay Open the Mind explicitly allows for calling up memories hidden by magic with a Clash of Wills, so I don't really think an ST ruling is needed there. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> I deliberately said Auspex 3, not Auspex 4. And I also said that it depends on how infallible STs allow Auspex to be, all they would have to do is put their hands on the person with the altered memory, ask a relevant question about what happened and they'll get a vision on what really happened, not the false memories that are recalled.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; Lying Mind doesn't even get a roll, so you can't exceptionally succeed on it. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Lying Mind must be used on a victim who they mesmerized first, so yes you technically can get an exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can roll an exceptional success on inflicting Mesmerize, which has its own set of effects. And Auspex 3 is for objects, so I assumed you typo'd the number. Auspex 3 has nothing to do with people or memories at all, so I'm unsure how it's relevant.<br /> <br /> In order to have any kind of meaningful discourse on an RPG, you kind of have to assume RAW/RAI in discussions. If you want to houserule stuff that's fine, but that's best left for a discussion explicitly about house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T03:36:46-08:00","id":841198,"title":"","content":"<br /> &lt;&lt; No, you can roll an exceptional success on inflicting Mesmerize, which has its own set of effects. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> If you don't successfully mesmerize someone, you aren't using the Lying Mind on them. Period. If you gain an exceptional success using Mesmerize on someone, your control is more fluid which translates into being able to install a command in that same turn AND make a slight alteration to their memory which the victim accepts as the truth. So yes, getting an exceptional success on someone in order to use the Lying Mind does make it more effective.<br /> <br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; And Auspex 3 is for objects, so I assumed you typo'd the number. And Auspex 3 is for objects, Auspex 3 has nothing to do with people or memories at all, so I'm unsure how it's relevant. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Maybe you should go back and reread the entire entry describing Auspex. Auspex 3 is an expansion of Auspex level 1 and level 2, expanded to include <b><i>places</i></b> and<i> <b>things</b></i>, not just people and grants additional situational bonuses to subsequent Auspex usage. <br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; In order to have any kind of meaningful discourse on an RPG, you kind of have to assume RAW/RAI in discussions. If you want to houserule stuff that's fine, but that's best left for a discussion explicitly about house rules. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> This statement is reductive bullshit. Everything regarding a role playing game involves houserules, since it's up to the participants to decide which rules they are going to use or discard. Which one of my parenthetical notations, outright statements indicating application of storyteller discretion of the application of mechanics <u><i>as written</i></u> told you I was employing a major deviation from the standing rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:52:59-08:00","id":841273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840976#post840976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ON Topic:<br /> Lashing out can end a command from Dominate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, physically lashing out as in punching them in the face can. As for lashing out with your beast, no it can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:59:59-08:00","id":841279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841273#post841273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for lashing out with your beast, no it can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mechanically, but it's clear Lashing Out is not meant to be simply a method of putting Conditions on people. Losing a struggle has an impact on characters. Ideally a further book will expand on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:20:52-08:00","id":841306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840976#post840976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ON Topic:<br /> Lashing out can end a command from Dominate?</div> </div> </div> </div> I mentioned that earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=840698#post840698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can't. You can lash out against all of Majesty, and half of Nightmare 1 (the non-illusion creating part). No other Discipline is affected by Lashing Out.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:51:28-08:00","id":841358,"title":"","content":"Lashing out and Disciplines: <br /> <br /> Majesty:<br /> <i>Another vampire can fortify herself against Awe with her predatory aura (see Lashing Out, p. 92). If she succeeds, she is unaffected by Awe.</i><br /> <br /> Only against Awe can you Lash out, Side effect, you need to be awed in order for the rest of Majesty to work. Pardon my french. If Awe works, you are Effed. Awe is subtle and you need to have a damn good reason to lash out. There is a whole thread about this.. Lashing out is violent and noticable. If you lash out against a vampire who is just naturally persuasive.. you might get yourself into a pickle..<br /> <br /> Nightmare:<br /> A vampire can lash outagainst this aura of fear with his predatory aura (see Lashing Out, p. 92). If he succeeds, he isn\u2019t affected by Dread Presence.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge it doesnt say anything about Lashing out in Dominate. I thought it did for Obfuscate too, but I cant seem to find the quote. So perhaps I was wrong on that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:57:41-08:00","id":841363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841358#post841358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my knowledge it doesnt say anything about Lashing out in Dominate. I thought it did for Obfuscate too, but I cant seem to find the quote. So perhaps I was wrong on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's well hidden, but i think you can lash out against Obfuscate. If my memory doesn't fail me, it's on the end of Cloak of Night(Obfuscate 3) text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 03-03-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T10:00:20-08:00","id":841366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841363#post841363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's well hidden, but i think you can lash out against Obfuscate. If my memory doesn't fail me, it's on the end of Cloak of Night(Obfuscate 3) text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> 'If another vampire manages to perceive him, through Auspex, attack, or any other means, she can sense his predatory aura and lash out. If she wins the predatory aura contest, Cloak of Night shatters, as does any other use of Obfuscate the vampire made.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T10:46:05-08:00","id":841382,"title":"","content":"If it's not strictly written, and it suits you, make it a house rule. The precedent is clearly there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T12:30:02-08:00","id":841433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841064#post841064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes but as the dominator has this weapon, the sire has his own weapon as well to use in order to conceal his plans. For example he could change the memory of his neonate if him were captured, putting the Ventrue astray. Or command to him, with dominate, to not talk or lie about something. In this case the Ventrue should win a clash of will comparing the successes of the neonate's sire with his own. And if the sire is an elder probably wins the contested roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I suppose a vampire who wants to keep a secret needs to take precautions against someone simply squeezing it out with mind-control. That, and I imagine confessions extracted using Disciplines might be treated with scepticism in vampire society. After all, who's to say the power can't be used to make some admit something that's not true?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T07:51:19-08:00","id":841886,"title":"","content":"The third best way to stop someone from giving up information under Dominate is to Dominate them yourself to forget the secret while being questioned by someone else.<br /> The second best way is to have blind servants/allies who are thus immune to Dominate.<br /> The best way is don't tell people secrets you don't want the court finding out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:00:07-08:00","id":841889,"title":"","content":"I believe there was a thread about being blind / no eyes and dominate still working. I am terrible at finding old threads, but I want to say that it's there and it works. I could be wrong. <br /> <br /> If you forget the information, what good is it to you anymore? How do you dominate yourself? Would you need a mirror to see yourself? Could you even give an order once you are mesmerized because you are hypnotized and waiting for orders? Personally. I dont think you should be able to mind roll yourself.<br /> <br /> You could dominate someone and command &quot;Speak only the truth&quot; and then everything after that should not be subject to skepticism. Every witness would know it to be truth. <br /> <br /> Dominated to forget and dominated to remember, if they were the same level dominate I would suggest a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:05:32-08:00","id":841896,"title":"","content":"You could also implant <i>slightly</i> false memories. Enough so that it seems like it happened, but concealing critical details.<br /> <br /> Or, if you don't have access to memory editing, just play around with signal to noise ratio. Flood sources and contacts with multiple versions of &quot;secrets&quot; so no one knows which one is actually true. Plus, it lets you know who has been spreading what. <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841889#post841889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there was a thread about being blind / no eyes and dominate still working. I am terrible at finding old threads, but I want to say that it's there and it works. I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>How, though? The base power requires eye contact. Kinda hard when you have no eyes (that work).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841889#post841889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you forget the information, what good is it to you anymore? How do you dominate yourself? Would you need a mirror to see yourself? Could you even give an order once you are mesmerized because you are hypnotized and waiting for orders? Personally. I dont think you should be able to mind roll yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can establish conditions, you might be able to make yourself &quot;remember&quot; it upon those conditions being triggered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841889#post841889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could dominate someone and command &quot;Speak only the truth&quot; and then everything after that should not be subject to skepticism. Every witness would know it to be truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you previously told them to consider another story as truth. Then, them telling the &quot;truth&quot; would include that fabrication.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-04-2016, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:16:38-08:00","id":841901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841886#post841886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way is don't tell people secrets you don't want the court finding out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Auspex, regular skills, there's tons of ways to find out secrets, dominate is really just one of many possibilities. The big thing is, you have to appreciate that players are going to be using their skills and abilities. You should avoid making plots that hinge on players not having agency. So they learn a secret, it's no big deal, then they just act on the secret and the story becomes about the results of that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> I think you want <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/46187-obfuscate-dominate\">this thread.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:22:52-08:00","id":841906,"title":"","content":"PCs will Fuck Shit Up <sup>TM</sup>. It's what they're for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T11:04:05-08:00","id":842002,"title":"","content":"Ah yes. I knew it was one sided. I was wrong on which side it was. Vampires dont have to see the victim's eyes but the Victim needs to see the vampire's. Thank you for finding that thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T11:17:54-08:00","id":842013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841889#post841889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there was a thread about being blind / no eyes and dominate still working. I am terrible at finding old threads, but I want to say that it's there and it works. I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> If you forget the information, what good is it to you anymore? How do you dominate yourself? Would you need a mirror to see yourself? Could you even give an order once you are mesmerized because you are hypnotized and waiting for orders? Personally. I dont think you should be able to mind roll yourself.<br /> <br /> You could dominate someone and command &quot;Speak only the truth&quot; and then everything after that should not be subject to skepticism. Every witness would know it to be truth.<br /> <br /> Dominated to forget and dominated to remember, if they were the same level dominate I would suggest a clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Vent0 covered this pretty well. You can command yourself to forget whatever information you want yourself to forget <i>until</i> you encounter such and such trigger you arrange for yourself to have. For example, you know you're meeting someone who also possesses a high level of Domination. Before you go to meet them you Dominate a servant into saying a certain obscure phrase to you when you return. After that you Dominate yourself into forgetting said info until you hear that phrase, so even if someone does try to extract the info from you during that meeting you don't actually know anything at the time, and it's only when you return and your servant speaks the triggering phrase will your full memory return.<br /> <br /> Now yes, this can potentially backfire pretty disastrously depending on circumstances, but it's a pretty solid strategy.<br /> <br /> And commanding someone to speak the truth only will only get them to answer what they believe is the truth, not necessarily what is objectively true. If they've been mind controlled (or even just convinced) into honestly thinking that something is true even when in reality it is false, ordering them to tell the truth is only going to get them to tell you the exact same thing that they would have told you anyways even if you didn't specify that they tell the truth, since they tell what they believe to be true anyways. You can't really order most people to tell the objective truth because not many people have the ability to know what is objectively true, and Dominate doesn't give that power to people who don't naturally have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T13:35:51-08:00","id":842121,"title":"","content":"Auspex allows you to read the thought of others even piercing magical alterations to someone's memories.<br /> Just wanted to point out a way around mind wipes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:15:01-08:00","id":842310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you forget the information, what good is it to you anymore? How do you dominate yourself? Would you need a mirror to see yourself? Could you even give an order once you are mesmerized because you are hypnotized and waiting for orders? Personally. I dont think you should be able to mind roll yourself. </div> </div> </div>Use Entombed Command to set up a trigger that makes you only remember while you're alone or something. It will be a Clash of Wills but hey it's another contested dice roll they have to get through to find out your secret. You can Dominate yourself by using Chain of Command on whoever or you can simply find another vampire with Dominate 4 and make them set up the trigger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842121#post842121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex allows you to read the thought of others even piercing magical alterations to someone's memories.<br /> Just wanted to point out a way around mind wipes.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but it is subject to Clash of Wills with whoever falsified the memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T01:04:01-08:00","id":842445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842310#post842310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use Entombed Command to set up a trigger that makes you only remember while you're alone or something. It will be a Clash of Wills but hey it's another contested dice roll they have to get through to find out your secret. You can Dominate yourself by using Chain of Command on whoever or you can simply find another vampire with Dominate 4 and make them set up the trigger.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> True but it is subject to Clash of Wills with whoever falsified the memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its the fact that it's a possibility they could be found out. <br /> Note im not saying its a bad idea. Hell the vampire who dominated himself to forget actually has the advantage. The fact that the effect last forever or the condition is meet. The dominated effect gets a plus four to its die pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T03:00:54-08:00","id":842462,"title":"","content":"How do people Dominate themselves? I've ran it as a &quot;I have a loyal ghoul who I trust the most and who has a dot of Dominate, and I trust him [or dominate him preemptively too] to do memory alterations and triggers that I need on myself&quot;, but I get a feeling from this conversation that it isn't really needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T03:04:16-08:00","id":842464,"title":"","content":"Actually may I ask, how is his dominate pool composed? That is what ranks does he have in the attributes and skills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T04:36:01-08:00","id":842481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842462#post842462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do people Dominate themselves? I've ran it as a &quot;I have a loyal ghoul who I trust the most and who has a dot of Dominate, and I trust him [or dominate him preemptively too] to do memory alterations and triggers that I need on myself&quot;, but I get a feeling from this conversation that it isn't really needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>A ghoul dominating their regnant isn't unnecessary, it's <i>impossible</i>. <br /> <br /> From page 297: &quot;When a Discipline would be contested or resisted by one of the Kindred, the ghoul may not add his Discipline dots to his own roll. <b>If he has any stage of blood bond to the vampire, the Discipline fails automatically</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> What people have suggested that might work is for the vampire to use Chain Of Command from page 142 with the intended target being themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T05:24:49-08:00","id":842491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842462#post842462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do people Dominate themselves? I've ran it as a &quot;I have a loyal ghoul who I trust the most and who has a dot of Dominate, and I trust him [or dominate him preemptively too] to do memory alterations and triggers that I need on myself&quot;, but I get a feeling from this conversation that it isn't really needed?</div> </div> </div> </div> Traditionally, people argue that you can use a mirror. Not sure if others have another way with the new rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:21:57-08:00","id":842546,"title":"","content":"It's clear that I need to add layers of complexity, but using Dominate as a counter might not work, since no one involved is a Ventrue. The gist of it is that one vampire accidentally Embraced a mortal, and to avoid taking the flak for it, tries to pin it on a rival. No real relation to the plot of the chronicle, but the PCs need to investigate it as a favour to someone who can supply them with other information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:26:28-08:00","id":842552,"title":"","content":"&quot;Who's your sire?&quot; is generally not something vampires have difficulty figuring out, blood sympathy and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:31:22-08:00","id":842553,"title":"","content":"Yes, which is why the Embraced vampire is in on the whole thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:37:29-08:00","id":842585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842462#post842462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do people Dominate themselves? I've ran it as a &quot;I have a loyal ghoul who I trust the most and who has a dot of Dominate, and I trust him [or dominate him preemptively too] to do memory alterations and triggers that I need on myself&quot;, but I get a feeling from this conversation that it isn't really needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much the mirror thing. Look into your own reflection in a mirror, mesmerize yourself, give yourself commands. I don't think it's covered in the 2e core so it's a bit ambiguous whether or not it's a thing, but I don't really have a problem with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:39:07-08:00","id":842586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842491#post842491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Traditionally, people argue that you can use a mirror. Not sure if others have another way with the new rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>'A vampire does not lack a reflection. You just never see her in the mirror. The Beast knows precisely where to stand.' I can't help but picture a vampire being shy with himself. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:51:38-08:00","id":842591,"title":"","content":"How is mirror different from a live feed from a camera? I'm asking honestly, I'm not sure what would be difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:00:40-08:00","id":842592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842591#post842591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is mirror different from a live feed from a camera? I'm asking honestly, I'm not sure what would be difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, really. The Lost Visage works on both. But in 2e it can be voluntarily turned off at no cost, so that shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't allow self-Dominate using mirrors or cameras. You could theoretically mesmerize yourself, but then you'd be mesmerized, which would make it kind of hard to give commands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:12:42-08:00","id":842599,"title":"","content":"I'm talking in context of:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . This contact [eye-contact for dominate] is possible through simple barriers like sunglasses (even mirrored) or tinted windows, but does not work when looking at a video feed rather than the vampire herself. </div> </div> </div>I've always thought that the spirit of this rule was to make sure that contact is between two different beings standing next to each other, face to face, not Skype conferences or something.<br /> Like...something can be between you and the target (&quot;barrier&quot;), but the target themselves has to be a real being, not any kind of projection of them (so no video conferences, mirror images, and so on). At least that's what I've thought; I'm not very familiar with previous incarnations of Dominate, so I don't have certain preassumptions in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:34:15-08:00","id":842607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842592#post842592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing, really. The Lost Visage works on both. But in 2e it can be voluntarily turned off at no cost, so that shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't allow self-Dominate using mirrors or cameras. You could theoretically mesmerize yourself, but then you'd be mesmerized, which would make it kind of hard to give commands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I call this the infinite retardation loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T10:33:35-08:00","id":842631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842599#post842599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking in context of:<br /> <br /> I've always thought that the spirit of this rule was to make sure that contact is between two different beings standing next to each other, face to face, not Skype conferences or something.<br /> Like...something can be between you and the target (&amp;quot;barrier&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but the target themselves has to be a real being, not any kind of projection of them (so no video conferences, mirror images, and so on). At least that's what I've thought; I'm not very familiar with previous incarnations of Dominate, so I don't have certain preassumptions in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I gotcha. My experience with 1st edition Requiem was entirely through LARP, so I don't know if this was different in tabletop, but the Mind's Eye Theater book for Requiem had a sidebar stating quite explicitly that Dominate required the victim to look the vampire in the <i>eye</i>. Not the nose, not the forehead, not the chin. Naturally, dark or mirrored sunglasses were a great defense against Domimate because if a would-be Dominate user can't see your eyes, they can't know if you're looking into theirs or not. This was a huge pain in the ass for everyone, and presumably has something to do with the decision to change it in 2e to say that it works as long as the victim <i>can see</i> the vampire's eyes, even through mirrored sunglasses. As for mirrors and cameras, I agree with your interpretation. I could see an argument for mirrors working though because it's the same light reflected from the vampire's eyes, just reflected again in the mirror, as opposed to their eyes on a video screen, which is light generated from the screen and merely an artificial representation of their eyes. But personally I rule that it's got to be direct, no reflections and no recordings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:16:47-08:00","id":842653,"title":"","content":"Yeah, vampire magic tends to rely more on symbolism than strict science. Moonlight doesn't count as sunlight even though it technically is, but no amount of artificial light will harm them at all, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T12:39:05-08:00","id":842686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842586#post842586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'A vampire does not lack a reflection. You just never see her in the mirror. The Beast knows precisely where to stand.' I can't help but picture a vampire being shy with himself. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>While Vampires can turn that off, I do like to indicate that they feel anxious when forced to stand within view of mirrors and the like. The Beast doesn't want to be noticed. Sending my party into a house of mirrors was fun. Though this is just a fun interpretation I enjoy, not really indicated in the rules directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:08:50-08:00","id":843240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842592#post842592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing, really. The Lost Visage works on both. But in 2e it can be voluntarily turned off at no cost, so that shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't allow self-Dominate using mirrors or cameras. You could theoretically mesmerize yourself, but then you'd be mesmerized, which would make it kind of hard to give commands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mesmerized only makes you quiet and subdued, it doesn't explicitly rob the victim of their ability to act, so I figure they'd be able to talk, albeit quietly and in a rather reserved manner. Enough to give yourself a command anyways.<br /> <br /> Moving on, let me first say that I think that auto-hypnosis via Dominate is a cool concept that allows neat tricks that reward creative thinking, and that as far as I can tell the game does nothing but benefit from its inclusion. Now as for why I would let a mirror would work while something like a video camera wouldn't, I justify it by the degrees of separation between the two. A mirror gives what I'd feel is a much more direct connection to the victim than something like a video feed, even a live one. Though even that could be diluted. While I would allow a single reflection to allow Domination (maybe at a penalty), once you get into hall of mirrors level of separation a mirror is no better than a video.<br /> <br /> That said, this is pretty much all personal opinion. The books as far as I know have nothing to say about this kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:22:28-08:00","id":843248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=843240#post843240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mesmerized only makes you quiet and subdued, it doesn't explicitly rob the victim of their ability to act, so I figure they'd be able to talk, albeit quietly and in a rather reserved manner. Enough to give yourself a command anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the reserved part that kills it for me. Domimate is about supplanting the victim's will with your own. That requires assertiveness and strength of character, two things that I don't think a Mesmerized character would have. Sure, they can talk, but I don't see them having the initiative to do so unless prompted, either by their master's command or by the situation demanding a verbal response. More importantly, even if they were able to say words, I don't see a mesmerized character being able to invest them with enough intention to constitute what I would call a command.<br /> <br /> But that's just me. I see nothing wrong with the interpretation that allows for auto-Dominate, even if it's not to my taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:52:22-08:00","id":843258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842592#post842592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing, really. The Lost Visage works on both. But in 2e it can be voluntarily turned off at no cost, so that shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't allow self-Dominate using mirrors or cameras. You could theoretically mesmerize yourself, but then you'd be mesmerized, which would make it kind of hard to give commands.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the point I brought up.. Once you were mesmerized.( your will crushed ). How do you impose the command ( impose your will). I would not allow one to dominate themselves. <br /> <br /> And a ghoul can't dominate their master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T22:26:23-08:00","id":843298,"title":"","content":"Personally I wouldn't allow Dominate through any form of non-direct eye contact, regardless of how tempting it is to do it just to recreate a certain Code Geass scene. LARPing it would be a pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T15:41:56-08:00","id":843644,"title":"","content":"If I allowed this, I'd have it have the potential to frenzy. You are essentially making your will supplicant to your own beast. Sounds dangerous if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:56:28-08:00","id":843684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=843644#post843644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I allowed this, I'd have it have the potential to frenzy. You are essentially making your will supplicant to your own beast. Sounds dangerous if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like that idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T19:54:06-08:00","id":843759,"title":"","content":"So everyone you dominate is at risk of frenzy? Why would it be any different for you than anyone else? The beast isn't the one giving commands.... You are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T20:07:03-08:00","id":843764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=843759#post843759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So everyone you dominate is at risk of frenzy? Why would it be any different for you than anyone else? The beast isn't the one giving commands.... You are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they just mean if you're, somehow, dominating yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T20:18:21-08:00","id":843769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=843759#post843759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So everyone you dominate is at risk of frenzy? Why would it be any different for you than anyone else? The beast isn't the one giving commands.... You are.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/41372-unhappy-with-b-s-assassination-by-obfuscate?p=41557#post41557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here may be a point to talk some theory. A lot of Disciplines work by manipulating the predatory aura, the feeling vampires give off of being <i>not right</i>. Sometimes that's terrifying, others it's alluring. Dominate, Majesty, and Nightmare are all &quot;pushing out,&quot; as Persephone Moore would put it. Obfuscate is about twisting it inward.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T06:19:06-08:00","id":843915,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, the accidental sire in this scenario is a Lancea member. Maybe they can use blood sorcery to protect the childe from disciplines that would ferret out the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T06:30:09-08:00","id":843917,"title":"","content":"You could always create a curse/blood magic that basically works like this:<br /> When you talk about subject X, or are about to say things Y, my wrath descends upon you, fucking up your shit and killing you (hardcore version) or hurting you badly.<br /> It's a classic in fiction where characters are going to get critical info by interrogating someone (&quot;no, please, anything but it, I cannot tell you, I beg you, noooOOOOOoooooooooooo dies&quot;), and it actually works mechanically, because again, it would deal damage and break the Mesmerize. It also feels very Lanceaish; break a promise and betray your master, FEEL THE RIGHTEOUS WRATH FOR YOUR SINS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T06:48:09-08:00","id":843926,"title":"","content":"I was going to have the Lancea member just give them bonus dice against any attempts to weasel out the truth, but that works much better. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T07:42:45-08:00","id":843955,"title":"","content":"Umm...wait, what's this about hunting down a sire? Okay, found it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=841002#post841002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm concerned about is that when the PCs need to extract information from a neonate (as a favour for some characters who have the information they need), the Ventrue will just Dominate him into telling them who his sire is. Kind of cuts the whole thing short. The best &quot;counter&quot; I've come up with is for the PC in question to acquire a reputation for overusing Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, a few issues here. Its insanely easy to figure out who the sire of someone is. Or, at least a very good way. Even if the memory of whom the sire was is erased, the childer can still use Blood Sympathy to figure it out. Taste of Family by testing blood gives a good estimate as well. Coil of the Voivoid might be able to do the same, I'll have to check. Auspex can simply use the level 3 effect to look back in the past. I'm sure there are others. Any one of these methods will work, alongside the Dominate effect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842546#post842546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's clear that I need to add layers of complexity, but using Dominate as a counter might not work, since no one involved is a Ventrue. The gist of it is that one vampire accidentally Embraced a mortal, and to avoid taking the flak for it, tries to pin it on a rival. No real relation to the plot of the chronicle, but the PCs need to investigate it as a favour to someone who can supply them with other information.</div> </div> </div> </div> All you need is one dot of Dominate to erase memories. Easy. Its not the new memories that are the problem, however. Its that they can be recovered.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm not really sure what your best course of action will be in this case. Hiding truth is generally fairly easy with enough clever moves. But there are just too many ways to hunt down who someone's sire is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T08:02:43-08:00","id":843966,"title":"","content":"I might just retcon the whole thing away, and give players some other information to find out. However, it's only a side-quest, so to speak. It's not supposed to take more than one session at most to figure out. Having the childe know perfectly well who their sire is, but be coerced and cursed with blood sorcery to be unable to speak the truth, feels like enough of a complication. The players will need to think outside the box a little, but should find it out once they manage to get their hands on one of those alternate solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T18:44:47-07:00","id":847958,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840252-dominate?p=842631#post842631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could see an argument for mirrors working though because it's the same light reflected from the vampire's eyes, just reflected again in the mirror, as opposed to their eyes on a video screen, which is light generated from the screen and merely an artificial representation of their eyes. But personally I rule that it's got to be direct, no reflections and no recordings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if reviving the discuss, esp. for a comment a page deep, is necromancy but the Mekhet devotion trend currently on the front page sent me <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/61745-walking-shadows-scathain-ars-speculorum\">here</a>, which is relevant.<br /> <br /> How?<br /> <br /> Well, according to the <span style=\"color:#000000\">Scathain, 'to understand the Grandest Lie, look in a mirror. You see yourself, don't you? Except that you don't. You see your </span><i>reflection</i><span style=\"color:#000000\">, which most certainly is not yourself'. Which is what Elfive was getting it but less symbolic and more occult truth of the vampire condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sharing because I thought the two trends brought together is neat, and opens an interesting new perspective on the whole 'mirror-doming' oneself. For example, conditioning yourself to forget certain information might seem to fail but has in fact conditioned your reflective self, giving you some protection against Scathains but angering your reflection or even Red Jack.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}